# API layer & errors (target state)

## Where code lives

- New HTTP clients belong in `src/api/<domain>.ts` with typed methods and endpoint constants
- Do **not** add to legacy `src/services/*` (high `any` debt) - migrate callers when touching them
- Components/pages never call raw `axiosInstance.get/post` for domain data - go through an API module + React Query
- When `side-actions.ts` grows past ~one concern, split by surface (e.g. `side-action-reports.ts`) and re-export from the umbrella module so callers stay stable
- Prefer deleting unused API methods over leaving clients that hit retired/410 endpoints

## Errors

- UI copy from `getErrorMessage` / `getApiErrorMessage` (`src/api/apiErrors.ts`), aligned with backend `build_error_body`
- `src/api/**` must stay `no-console` clean (CI `lint:api`); use `devLog` / `devError` for diagnostics

## Payloads

- PATCH through `normalizePatchPayload` - `undefined` omitted, explicit `null` clears fields
- Use `skip403Redirect` on probes (e.g. director-access) when the UI handles 403 inline

## Axios

Treat `src/api/axios.ts` as delicate infrastructure (auth refresh, redirects, slash normalization). Prefer extending domain API modules over adding more global side effects to the instance.
